WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.471
Synthetic media includes generated or altered images, video, audio, text, documents, and screenshots.

00:00:07.471 --> 00:00:18.548
Deepfakes can represent people, events, actions, or statements, but not every edit, suspicious artifact, or false caption is a deepfake.

00:00:18.548 --> 00:00:26.019
Misleading media can be fully synthetic, partly manipulated, staged, or genuine but miscontextualized.

00:00:26.019 --> 00:00:35.551
Visual and audio warning signs help form questions, yet compression and ordinary processing can create similar artifacts.

00:00:35.551 --> 00:00:39.930
Absence of artifacts does not prove authenticity.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:49.977
Verification combines provenance, source history, reverse image comparison, keyframes, metadata, timelines, location or time clues, and independent corroboration.

00:00:49.977 --> 00:00:58.479
Detection tools remain one fallible input with false positives, false negatives, drift, and platform effects.

00:00:58.479 --> 00:01:03.889
Responsible reporting distinguishes unverified, manipulated, synthetic, and miscontextualized content.

00:01:03.889 --> 00:01:11.875
It states evidence, confidence, limitations, and alternative explanations while protecting sensitive people and material.

00:01:11.875 --> 00:01:18.315
The goal is disciplined analysis rather than panic or instant certainty.

00:01:18.315 --> 00:01:30.423
Preserve context, test claims, communicate carefully, and use media verification to support accountable decisions without creating additional reputational, privacy, or safety harm.
